.TH DEVTOOL 1 "2026-07-11" "devtool 0.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devtool \- generic Unix developer helper CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devtool
.RI [ global-options ] command " [command-options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
devtool applies artifacts, validates repositories, records transactional rollback state,
summarizes restore/build/test output, copies results, and publishes one live run to a
desktop HUD or the Android Devtool Frontend.
.PP
One mutating devtool run is allowed per repository. A second invocation fails immediately
while the current operation owns the repository run lock. There are no concurrency modes,
wait policies, or path-scoped leases.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B restore | build | test | validate | wine-validate | run | package
Run project actions from .devtool.toml or detected project defaults.
.TP
.B validate
Run restore, build, and test. Dotnet validation uses
.B dotnet build --no-restore
after restore and
.B dotnet test --no-build
after build.
.TP
.B apply-overlay | apply-overlays | apply-snapshot
Apply an artifact transactionally. Options include
.BR --validate ,
.BR --preview ,
.BR --diff ,
.BR --interactive ,
.BR --commit ,
.BR --skip-restore ,
.BR --skip-build ,
and
.BR --skip-test .
.TP
.B batch
Run a sequence of devtool steps.
.TP
.B status | doctor | detect | handoff | history | rollback | targets
Inspect or maintain repository state.
.TP
.B hud
Run the terminal, web, studio, desktop, or Android app bridge renderer.
.TP
.B android-hud-bridge
Forward shared Termux/chroot live state to the Android app.
.TP
.B commit | tag | release-notes
Git helper commands. Commit, tag, and rollback use the same repository run lock.
.TP
.B ai-prompt | completion | logs | init-config | config
Generate workflow text, shell completion, inspect logs, or configure devtool.
.SH ANDROID FRONTEND
The CLI publishes Android progress only through
.BR --hud-mode android-bridge .
The Android app owns its live notification, optional floating overlay, visual frontend,
history, Termux command execution, and native Tasker plug-in integration.
.PP
The former standalone Termux notification mode and CLI Tasker/notification flags have been
removed. Use the app settings and Tasker plug-in action instead.
.SH TERMUX CHROOT RUNNER
The optional host-side commands
.B devtool-androidos
and
.B devtool-termux-chroot
forward devtool invocations into a named chroot. The command shape is:
.PP
.B sudo chrootctl --name androidos exec -- zsh -lc '<command>'
.PP
Host paths are translated for the chroot. Desktop HUD names are adapted to
.B android-bridge
when execution originates from Termux.
.SH TRANSACTIONAL APPLY
Before mutating files, devtool backs up only paths touched by the artifact. If extraction,
restore, build, test, commit preparation, or interruption fails, the touched paths are
restored. A successful rollback is reported as recovery while the final result retains the
actual phase that failed.
.PP
A stale transaction left by a killed process is restored before the next mutating command,
which then exits non-zero so the requested operation can be rerun.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -r , " --repo" " PATH"
Repository root.
.TP
.BR -y , " --yes"
Assume yes for confirmations.
.TP
.BR --force
Allow explicitly forced dangerous operations.
.TP
.BR --copy , " --copy-summary" , " --copy-json"
Copy raw output, the rendered summary, or JSON.
.TP
.BR --auto-hud , " --hud-mode" " MODE"
Start or reuse the selected live HUD. Use
.B android-bridge
for the Android app.
.TP
.BR --no-hud
Do not publish live HUD progress for this command.
.TP
.BR --hud-overlay
Request the app's user-enabled floating overlay for this run.
.TP
.BR --hud-no-overlay
Keep the run in the app without opening the floating overlay.
.TP
.BR --machine "[=compact|pretty]" , " --machine-file" " FILE"
Emit or save the machine JSON envelope.
.TP
.BR --performance , " --performance-file" " FILE"
Write wall time, per-operation durations, process count, and peak RSS metrics as JSON.
.SH TARGET SELECTION
Named targets are never selected implicitly. Legacy default_target and project.target values are ignored; use --target, --solution, or artifact target metadata.
.SH REMOVED OPTIONS
.BR --notify ,
.BR --notify-progress ,
.BR --tasker ,
.BR --tasker-progress ,
.BR --tasker-broadcast ,
.BR --concurrency ,
.BR --lock-timeout ,
and
.B --no-wait
are no longer accepted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/devtool/logs
Saved command logs.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/devtool/locks
Single-run repository lock files.
.TP
.I .devtool.toml
Per-repository configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_XDG_DIR
Override devtool runtime state storage.
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_RUN_ID
Run identity shared with the Android app or desktop HUD.
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_HUD_SINGLETON
Controls reuse of the HUD process; use
.B kill
to replace an older renderer.
.SH AUTHOR
OpenAI
